WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:15.940
Fire And Blood will reign again and you can
expect to see the Blackfyre Rebellions in

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:21.040
the later seasons of House of the Dragon,
which thus of course inludes legendary Bittersteel

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.540
as well,
the man behind almost every Blackfyre Rebellion.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.600
The upcoming Game of Thrones prequel series,
House of the Dragon, is based on the George

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.930
RR Martin's Targaryen history book Fire &amp; Blood.
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:38.120
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president
to air in 2022.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:43.610
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve
as showrunners and executive producers. George

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.240
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive
producer.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:52.680
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.330
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the

00:00:56.330 --> 00:01:01.190
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:05.940
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.820
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”
In other words it covers events from Aegon's

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:15.080
Conquest to the Dance of the Dragons.
Thats Fire And Blood volume 1.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:19.340
House of the Dragon will start with a build
up towards the Dance of the Dragons and early

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:24.490
seasons will cover the Dance itself. Later
seasons however, will be based on George RR

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:27.659
Martin’s yet unfinished Fire And Blood volume
2 book .

00:01:27.659 --> 00:01:33.130
The yet unreleased Fire And Vlood volume 2
will continue from where part 1 ended, with

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:38.570
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:44.320
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.869
One of the key characters and according to
some,

00:01:46.869 --> 00:01:50.060
the true mastermind behind the Blackfyre Rebellions
was Bittersteel.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:55.799
Ser Aegor Rivers, frequently called Bittersteel,
was one of the infamous four Great Bastards

00:01:55.799 --> 00:02:01.210
and a son of a King Aegon IV Targaryen, also
known as "Aegon the Unworthy".

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:07.030
The four Great Bastards were Daemon Blackfyre
(whose mother, secretly, was Daena Targaryen),

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:11.070
Aegor "Bittersteel" Rivers (whose mother was
a member of House Bracken),

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:15.160
Brynden "Bloodraven" Rivers (whose mother
was a member of House Blackwood),

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:21.659
and Shiera Seastar (whose mother was Serenei
of Lys, from an ancient Valyrian noble family).

00:02:21.659 --> 00:02:27.310
On his deathbed, Aegon IV foolishly (and perhaps
spitefully) had them all legitimized,

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:31.620
which led to strife between them and his legitimate
heir King Daeron II,

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.940
tensions which ultimately split the realm
apart in the devastating civil war known as

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:41.250
the Blackfyre Rebellion. Aegor was a Blackfyre
loyalist and the founder of a famed group

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:46.190
of exiled sellswords,
the Golden Company composed primarily of Westerosi

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:51.450
exiles. In his personal arms, he combined
the red stallion of House Bracken with black

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:55.159
dragon wings from House Blackfyre, on a golden
field.

00:02:55.159 --> 00:02:59.269
Being a half-Targaryen, Aegor had purple eyes,
but black hair.

00:02:59.269 --> 00:03:04.549
He looked like a warrior, being lean, light,
and tall. Aegor's armor was well-made, although

00:03:04.549 --> 00:03:10.470
plain-looking, being grey-steel and black
rings. On his helm was a horse head with a

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:16.360
horse's mane flowing behind. His shield displayed
his personal sigil: a stallion with black

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:20.269
dragon wings, on a golden field, snorting
fire.

00:03:20.269 --> 00:03:25.319
Aegor was angry all of his life, and quickly
irritated and offended. He did not smile,

00:03:25.319 --> 00:03:31.269
and especially loathed his younger half-brother,
Brynden Rivers known as the Bloodraven.

00:03:31.269 --> 00:03:36.349
Aegor was born at King's Landing to one of
King Aegon IV Targaryen's mistresses, Barba

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:39.510
Bracken.
When Queen Naerys Targaryen recovered her

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:42.459
health,
Prince Daeron and Aemon the Dragonknight forced

00:03:42.459 --> 00:03:47.840
Aegon to send Barba and child from the capital,
and Aegor was instead raised at Stone Hedge

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.560
in the riverlands.
Aegor loathed Brynden even further when Shiera

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:55.959
Seastar, their beautiful half-sister
and a fellow Great Bastard, chose Brynden

00:03:55.959 --> 00:03:59.060
over him.
Bloodraven asked her to marry him dozens of

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:03.040
times and she refused,
but she did let him into her bed - although

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:08.709
she had many lovers. Shiera, however, completely
rejected Bittersteel, and for this he never

00:04:08.709 --> 00:04:12.690
forgave Bloodraven.
It also did not help that Bittersteel's mother

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:16.340
was a Bracken
and Bloodraven's mother was a Blackwood, as

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:20.510
those two noble families had been feuding
for thousands of years.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:24.200
Bittersteel became a great champion and general
for the Blackfyres,

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:28.450
while Bloodraven became a great champion and
general for the Targaryens.

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:33.550
Their other half-brother, Daemon Blackfyre,
agreed to wed his daughter Calla to Aegor.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:37.330
Aegor often urged Daemon to press his own
claim to the Iron Throne.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:41.740
''Bittersteel and Bloodraven both loved Shiera
Seastar, and the Seven Kingdoms bled.''

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:46.860
are thoughts of Ser Barristan Selmy, indicating
that the true reason behind Bittersteel persuing

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:53.020
Daemon to rebel against their Targaryen half-brother,
was just so he could fight and kill Bloodraven.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:58.470
In the First Blackfyre Rebellion in 196 AC,
Aegor was the right hand of Daemon Blackfyre

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:04.030
against King Daeron II Targaryen. In addition,
it's rumored he convinced Daemon to start

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:07.780
the rebellion.
During the battle of the Redgrass Field, Aegor

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:12.800
commanded the right of Daemon's host.
To prevent a rout upon Daemon's death during

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:18.230
the battle, Aegor rallied his troops and charged
into the Raven's Teeth, the archers of Brynden

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:23.940
Rivers, who just killed Daemon and his sons.
Although Aegor took out Bloodraven's eye during

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.570
their duel,
he ultimately fled the battlefield when the

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:30.730
Targaryen reinforcement came and the deafeat
was certain.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:35.800
Carrying the Valyrian steel sword Blackfyre,
Aegor fled Westeros with Daemon's widow,

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:41.920
Rohanne of Tyrosh, and her surviving children,
eventually settling in the Free City of Tyrosh.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:45.810
While in the Free Cities, Aegor served a year
with the Second Sons before leaving

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:51.410
to create the Golden Company, a famous mercenary
organization, to stop the loss of support

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:57.750
for the Blackfyres as many of Bittersteel's
remaining men deserted to join mercenary companies.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:02.940
In response, Bittersteel resorted to forming
his remaining soldiers into their own mercenary

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:08.120
company, called the Golden Company. Wars cost
money and Aegor Rivers, the leader of the

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:12.840
Blackfyre forces, decided he could sell his
army's services to other lords while waiting

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:16.750
to return to Westeros.
The Golden Company was born.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:21.150
Day by day and year by year they fought in
petty wars between different Free Cities in

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:25.850
order to make enough money for their basic
upkeep. This step at least ensured

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:30.780
that the Blackfyre Pretenders would have some
semblance of a stable core fighting force

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.990
whenever they mounted a new plot to invade
Westeros.

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:38.730
While sellswords are notoriously unreliable,
the Golden Company has a respectable reputation.

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:43.710
They are said to have never broken a contract.
The words of the Golden Company are "Beneath

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:48.360
the gold, the bitter steel", and refer to
Aegor's nickname, Bittersteel,

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:51.080
to remind themselves that they are not just
sellswords,

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:54.600
but knights of the Seven Kingdoms who will
one day retake their home.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:59.270
Shortly after its creation, and under Aegor's
command, the Golden Company became one of

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:03.980
the most famous and disciplined sellsword
companies known in the Free Cities. They quickly

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:09.260
established their reputation by sacking Qohor
when the city refused to honor its contract.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:14.350
From the Free Cities, Bittersteel continued
to plot new invasions of the Seven Kingdoms

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:18.690
for at least forty years. The Golden Company
was heavily involved in three of the four

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:23.221
Blackfyre Rebellions that followed the first
one. After the first (and greatest) rebellion

00:07:23.221 --> 00:07:27.970
failed in 196 AC,
he took no part in the Second Blackfyre Rebellion

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:33.710
in 212 AC - which was more of a failed plot
than an actual war - which was instigated

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:39.570
by Daemon II Blackfyre. Daemon was kept in
captivity rather than executed with the other

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:45.220
rebel leaders, ensuring that Aegor Rivers
could not name his brother Haegon as a serious

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:50.070
pretender. However, Daemon died a few years
later while a hostage in the Red Keep,

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:53.740
and Haegon and Bittersteel launched the Third
Blackfyre Rebellion.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:59.320
While Aegor refused to support Daemon II Blackfyre
during the Second Blackfyre Rebellion in 211

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:02.971
AC,
he supported Haegon I Blackfyre in the Third

00:08:02.971 --> 00:08:08.310
Blackfyre Rebellion in 219 AC.
During one of the various Blackfyre Rebellions,

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:13.440
Aegor swore a blood oath with Torwyn Greyjoy,
but this Lord Reaper of Pyke betrayed Aegor

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:17.130
to his enemies.
Aegor was captured at the end of the third

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:22.060
rebellion, and was briefly taken captive after
the failure of the Third Blackfyre Rebellion,

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:26.800
and brought to the Red Keep in chains.
He was found guilty of high treason, and while

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:32.279
Bloodraven and Prince Aerion urged King Aerys
I Targaryen to execute Bittersteel, Aerys

00:08:32.279 --> 00:08:36.650
instead chose to send him to the Wall;
however, Aegor's allies captured the ship

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:41.210
transporting him to Eastwatch-by-the-Sea
and freed him to return to Essos and to the

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:45.269
Golden Company.
In Tyrosh, before the year was over, Aegor

00:08:45.269 --> 00:08:49.740
crowned Daemon III Blackfyre, Haegon I's eldest
son.

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:55.769
In 236 AC, Aegor landed on Westeros at the
head of the Golden Company with Daemon III,

00:08:55.769 --> 00:09:01.200
starting the Fourth Blackfyre Rebellion. By
this time, however, they had very little support.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:06.129
The rebellion was crushed at the battle of
Wendwater Bridge, although Aegor managed to

00:09:06.129 --> 00:09:08.899
escape.
Daemon III Blackfyre was personally killed

00:09:08.899 --> 00:09:12.670
by Ser Duncan the Tall in battle and the rebellion
ended.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:16.250
This was the last Blackfyre rebellion Aegor's
participated in,

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:20.129
but there was one more, named the War of the
Ninepenny Kings.

00:09:20.129 --> 00:09:24.850
A few years after the Wendwater Bridge, Aegor
reappeared in the Disputed Lands,

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:28.160
where he fell during a skirmish between Tyrosh
and Myr.

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:32.319
On his deathbed, he commanded the men of the
Golden Company to boil the flesh from his

00:09:32.319 --> 00:09:35.050
skull,
dip it in gold, and carry it before them when

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:40.410
they cross the narrow sea to retake Westeros.
Beneath the gold, the bitter steel, indeed.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:46.329
The captains-general who have since led the
Golden Company have followed Aegor's example.

00:09:46.329 --> 00:09:49.750
Legendary characters such as Bittersteel,
Daemon Blackfyre, the Dragonknight

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:53.910
and a dozen more legendary characters coming
before in the Dance of the Dragons

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:58.661
and after in Roberts Rebellion, legendary
battles such as each Blackfyre Rebellion

00:09:58.661 --> 00:10:03.470
and many more coming before and after as well,
especially all the battles in the Targaryen

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:06.370
civil war,
all of that and more this Game of Thrones

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:10.129
prequel show, House of the Dragon, brings
in 2022 on HBO.

00:10:10.129 --> 00:10:13.269
Thank you so much for watching, I hope you
enjoyed this video and if you did please give

00:10:13.269 --> 00:10:21.299
it a big thumbs up and I hope to see you in
the next one. Peace!

